WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.799
How can a movie make $400 million, and still
be a box office bomb?

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:08.139
According to Dwayne Johnson, it can't be.

00:00:08.139 --> 00:00:11.500
This is the Black Adam box office controversy
explained.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.460
The year was 2007.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:18.520
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson's Hollywood career
was only beginning to gain traction, and superhero-centric

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.500
movies were far from the surefire cinematic
moneymakers they'd soon become.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.050
Nevertheless, it was announced that the longtime
WWE sensation would star in a big-screen comic

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:33.140
book adaptation focused on Shazam — but
he wouldn't portray the tenured print hero.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.820
Rather, he'd take on the role of his greatest
enemy, Teth-Adam, better known as Black Adam.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.910
"There's no one on this planet that can stop
me."

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.520
Around 15 years after he first signed on for
the role, Johnson finally got to play "The

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.460
Man in Black" in 2022.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.180
So was it the change in the hierarchy of power
in the DC Universe that Johnson promised?

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.080
Well, critics didn't much care for Black Adam,
but general audiences seem to have been happy

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.440
enough with the movie.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.699
However, things aren't looking too great at
the box office.

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:08.100
The film is hovering around the $400 million
mark worldwide, and according to some controversial

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.369
reports, that makes the movie a box office
bomb.

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:15.740
You're probably wondering how could the film
be a bomb with a wide world gross as impressive

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.740
as that.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.690
As some outlets are alleging, it all comes
down to the movie's budget.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:27.229
As laid out by Variety, Black Adam cost around
$195 million to produce, but the costs don't

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:28.260
stop there.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.910
You also have to account for the film's marketing
budget, which most agree sits somewhere between

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.909
$80 and $100 million.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:41.190
On the high end, that's in the neighborhood
of $300 million — but we're still not done.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:45.299
After all, it costs money to get a film like
Black Adam in theaters — around half of

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:48.159
the cash accumulated due to ticket sales.

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:53.610
According to a bombshell report by Variety,
Black Adam will have to make around $600 million

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.110
globally in order to break even.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.600
That's taking into account the film's budget,
its marketing push, and movie theaters' share

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.229
of the profits.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:04.049
According to Variety's financial sources,
at the rate the film is going, it will be

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:05.049
lucky to get out of the $400 million territory.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:06.720
That means Black Adam is on track to lose
millions.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.000
After that report was made public, sources
close to Warner Bros. indicated to /Film that

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.300
Variety's initial report is inaccurate, and
that the break-even point for "Black Adam"

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:23.019
is $425 million, not $600 million – so the
movie still stands a chance of breaking even

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:24.760
when the final numbers roll in.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.680
That was corroborated with a report by Deadline,
whose film finance sources called the claims

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.440
of 'Black Adam's failure 'simply not true.'

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:39.280
According to Deadline, the film is on track
to profit somewhere between $52 and $72 million.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.180
Dwayne Johnson, Black Adam himself, also weighed
in on the controversy, trumpeting Black Adam's

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.550
success and comparing the movie's grosses
to the first 'Captain America' movie, which

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:52.840
netted $370 million globally in 2011.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.769
One question remains, though: What went wrong
to make 'Black Adam's' success so debatable?

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:03.280
Black Adam was released on October 21st, 2022,
and over the course of that weekend, it did

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.599
pretty well for itself.

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:10.150
Globally, it took in just under $143 million,
a much better performance than the opening

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.500
weekend of Shazam!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.670
back in late March 2019.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.670
As the weeks went on, however, the movie progressively
took in less and less — a phenomenon hardly

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.409
uncommon in the film world.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:25.430
However, things went from bad to worse for
Black Adam during the week of November 11th,

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:29.790
since it had no choice but to compete against
a juggernaut in the comic book movie world:

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.049
Black Panther: Wakanda Forever.

00:03:32.049 --> 00:03:33.560
"Wakanda Forever!"

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.060
"Wakanda Forever!"

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.709
Director Ryan Coogler's latest foray into
the Marvel Cinematic Universe came out swinging

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:41.370
during its opening weekend.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:47.680
The long-awaited sequel to 2018's Black Panther
made a staggering $330 million in its opening

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.845
weekend, pushing Black Adam into the second
highest-earner spot after weeks at number one.

00:03:52.845 --> 00:03:57.510
Dwayne Johnson himself even acknowledged the
box office defeat, congratulating the Wakanda

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.980
Forever team on Twitter as well as Instagram
and admitting that the Marvel Studios sequel

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.930
gave Black Adam a run for its money at the
box office.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.110
That wasn't the end of Black Adam's woes,
though.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:13.150
After all, it's no secret that, after years
on the entertainment scene, the MCU is a slick,

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.159
well-oiled machine.

00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:18.880
The films and television shows fit together
nicely, the actors stick around, and there's

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.290
a consistent vision behind the entire franchise.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:26.130
Thus, when it comes to characters, heavy hitters
and niche favorites alike stand a chance to

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.090
lead successful projects.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.190
On the other hand, DC films have faced a perpetual
identity crisis for years, with the slate

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:38.320
full of new entries into the already-struggling
DC Extended Universe, standalone experiments,

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.060
and franchise starters.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.630
Suffice to say, it's a bit of a jumbled mess.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:47.680
Thankfully, James Gunn and Peter Safran are
now at the helm of DC Studios: a Warner Bros.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.210
Discovery subdivision designed to keep DC
productions on the right track.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.560
But it'll take some time for this initiative
to really kick into high gear.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.960
For years, fans have been jerked around with
recasts, retries, story inconsistencies, and

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.710
more, which have made it difficult to go out
and enjoy most DC movies.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.690
It'll take time to rebuild goodwill among
fans.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:13.470
But even amid the financial controversy and
relatively lukewarm reviews, "Black Adam"

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.020
inching into the black at the box office would
be a solid enough first step.

